Port patch 0039 - cheat: the Hall of Fame can be shown complete (all 151 Pokemon), which plays the completion scene
Why: a requested feature of the port (an option in the Options menu, off by default; KYUJO_CHEAT_HOF=1 for one run). The Hall of Fame (Victory Palace) lists a Pokemon only when the save holds a
record for it (VictoryPalace_LoadSpeciesRecord reads typed record 0x13, one per species); VictoryPalace_CheckAllCaught plays the completion scene (State_VictoryPalace -> Stage_RunDemoScene(0x1A)) when
all 151 are present and the "seen it" flag (Save_GetOptionsField1F) is not set yet. Collecting all 151 takes a very long time, so with the cheat switched on a species WITHOUT a record gets one that
is made up in memory when it is asked for: the first cup (unk_00 = 1), level 50, ID 00000, the species name as the nickname (Text_CopySpeciesName) and the player's own name as the trainer
(Text_GetPlayerLabel(1)), so the gallery shows it as the player's. Real records are never replaced, nothing is written to the save by this function: switching the cheat off shows the real Hall again.
(What the real game then does is unchanged: after the completion scene it stores its own "seen" flag and the chosen Pokemon in the save, as it does after a genuine completion.)
The host decides (__osHostCheatOption(1), host_cheat.c).
Files: `src/pokemon_stats.c`

